  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Between the Estérel massif and the sea, the Agay and Anthéor area of Saint-Raphaël has several campsites and a holiday village whose tourist office listings say "animals accepted". This page gathers the conditions each one publishes for your dog.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you book</h2>
      <p>The conditions for welcoming dogs (size, breed, supplement, season) vary from one place to another: a direct call before booking is still the safest approach. Here is what each place's website or the Saint-Raphaël and Estérel Côte d'Azur tourist office listings publish:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Esterel Caravaning</strong> (5 stars, Agay): according to its own FAQ, dogs of all sizes are accepted on pitches and in mobile homes, with no restriction on breed or category (categories 1 and 2 included), with a €5 per night surcharge in high season only; dogs on a leash in common areas and not allowed in the pools. Address: 4481 avenue des Golfs, Agay. The sandy beach of Agay bay is 3 km from the campsite (30 minutes on foot according to the site, or 5 minutes by car). The site announces the 2027 season from 20 March to 25 September.</li>
        <li><strong>Les Mas de l'Estérel</strong> (3-star holiday village, Agay): "dogs accepted outside July-August", with a surcharge, according to the tourist office (04 94 19 11 00, avenue du Cap Roux, Agay). The listing mentions direct access to the Estérel hiking trails.</li>
        <li><strong>Azur Rivage</strong> (2-star campsite, Anthéor): animals accepted with a surcharge, including in rentals, according to the tourist office (04 94 44 83 12, 1785 boulevard des Lucioles); open from 1 May to 30 September 2026, with the sea less than 300 m away according to the listing.</li>
        <li><strong>Agay Soleil</strong> (campsite, Agay): animals accepted with a surcharge according to the tourist office (04 94 82 00 79, 1152 boulevard de la plage); the listing does not say whether animals are allowed in the mobile homes: ask before booking a rental. Open from 16 March to 1 November 2026, with direct access to a small sandy beach.</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: beach rules for dogs vary from one town to another: check the beach pages for the area before settling on the sand.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>All four places are close to the Estérel massif, whose hiking trails are accessible from Les Mas de l'Estérel.</p>
